      "text": "Singapore’s air quality is **unhealthy to very unhealthy** in the latest NEA readings I found. At **1:00 a.m. Singapore time on October 16**, 1-hour PM2.5 ranged from **107 µg/m³ in the North** to **170 µg/m³ in the Central region**; West was 152, East 139, and South 112. ([api-open.data.gov.sg](https://api-open.data.gov.sg/v2/real-time/api/pm25))\n\nThe latest 24-hour PSI readings were **132–203** across regions—**Unhealthy** in the North, South, West and East, and **Very Unhealthy** in Central. ([api-open.data.gov.sg](https://api-open.data.gov.sg/v2/real-time/api/psi))",
